{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChL89oJzfq4XnK5ooMgm4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `saveAll` in `store.js`, and the existing test passes.\n\nThe cause was that `items.forEach(async ...)` doesn't wait for the async callbacks. `saveAll` returned the count right away, while the `db.put` calls were still running. A failed write also became an unhandled rejection instead of making `saveAll` reject.\n\nIt now does `await Promise.all(items.map((item) => db.put(item.id, item)))`. `saveAll` resolves with the count only after every write finishes, and it rejects if any write fails. The writes still run in parallel, as before. If your db needs them in order or rate-limited, a sequential `for...of` loop with `await` would do that instead.\n\nThe existing test only checks the happy path. I didn't add a test for the early-resolve or rejection cases."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":554,"cache_read_input_tokens":22546,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":554},"output_tokens":258,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92e72d00-11bd-4127-8b62-0a6ceffac842","uuid":"e811e97b-7305-4b1e-9e46-b702fbc8b2ce","timestamp":"2026-11-23T15:49:26.453Z","request_id":"req_011ChL89o7atptpMBDjnQoCZ"}
